message_4.text:
その通りです。$P(A)$ は**事前確率**、つまり新しい観察結果やテスト結果を考慮する前の、ベースラインとなる初期の確信度を指します。先ほどの健康診断の例では、一般人口における割合である $1\%$ がこれにあたります。

---

### チャレンジ問題：直感チェック

ベイズの定理が実際にはどのように機能するか、あなたの直感を試す簡単なシナリオを用意しました：

```interactive_question
{
  "type": "choice",
  "id": "bayes_intuition_quiz_2",
  "multiple": false,
  "question": "Suppose a burglar alarm goes off in a neighborhood. If burglary is extremely rare in that area (a very tiny prior probability), what is typically true about the posterior probability that a break-in actually occurred, assuming the alarm has a non-zero false alarm rate?",
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "opt_very_high",
      "text": "The posterior probability is close to 100% because alarms are specifically built to detect break-ins."
    },
    {
      "id": "opt_counterintuitively_low",
      "text": "The posterior probability may remain surprisingly low because false alarms from normal events outnumber true break-ins."
    },
    {
      "id": "opt_equal_to_prior",
      "text": "The posterior probability remains completely unchanged regardless of whether the alarm sounds."
    },
    {
      "id": "opt_independent",
      "text": "The posterior probability depends only on alarm volume, not the baseline frequency of burglaries."
    }
  ]
}
```

